-- title:
--   The erasure region is an endpoint time-sharing segment plus unit conversions
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal C(\mathcal N)\subseteq\mathbb R^3$ be the closure of net triples $(R,P,S)$ achievable with vanishing full trace-norm error by finite block protocols using independent channel copies, forward noiseless public and private classical communication, and initially uniform shared secret key. Generated and consumed rates are separately finite and fixed before the error tolerances. Positive net rates mean generation. The uniform private message and generated secret key must be jointly recovered and decoupled from all public data, the full channel environment, and explicitly discarded local systems. Local memory and operations are free; there is no feedback or prior entanglement.
--
--   For the qubit erasure channel with $\epsilon\in[0,1]$, let $\mathcal U$ be the cone generated by $(0,-1,1)$, $(-1,1,-1)$, and $(1,-1,0)$. Then
--   $$
--   \mathcal C(\mathcal N_\epsilon)=\left\{(1-t)(1-\epsilon,0,0)+t(0,1-\epsilon,-\epsilon)+u:
--   0\le t\le1,\ u\in\mathcal U\right\}.
--   $$
--   The two endpoints are the publicly-enhanced private father rates for entropy parameters $H_2(p)=0$ and $H_2(p)=1$. Thus time sharing between these endpoints, followed by unit-resource conversions, gives the full region. The region is not just the bounded segment; for $\epsilon\ge1/2$ the second endpoint is dominated. Here $H_2$ is binary entropy in bits and its input parameter ranges over $[0,1/2]$.
-- source:
--   Public and private resource trade-offs for a quantum channel, arXiv:1005.3818v3, PDF p. 20, Figure 5

import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Claimed50_P24

noncomputable section

open scoped Matrix ComplexConjugate

namespace QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Claimed50.P24

open QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Information100.P67
  (IsIsometry receiverChannel complementaryChannel erasureDilation)

attribute [local instance] Classical.propDecidable Classical.decEq

variable {I B E J D F : Type}

variable [Fintype I] [Fintype B] [Fintype E] [Fintype J] [Fintype D] [Fintype F]

variable [DecidableEq I] [DecidableEq B] [DecidableEq E]

variable [DecidableEq J] [DecidableEq D] [DecidableEq F]

variable [Nonempty I] [Nonempty B] [Nonempty E]

variable [Nonempty J] [Nonempty D] [Nonempty F]

/-- Figure 5, PDF p.20, pinned by Theorem 6, p.19: the full region is time sharing
between father endpoints (1-eps,0,0) and (0,1-eps,-eps), plus the unit conversion cone.
For eps >= 1/2 the second endpoint is dominated; the expression still holds. -/
theorem erasureTimeSharing (eps : ℝ) (he0 : 0 ≤ eps) (he1 : eps ≤ 1) :
    privateDynamicRegion (erasureDilation (A := Fin 2) eps) = {r | ∃ t : ℝ, t ∈ Set.Icc 0 1 ∧
      ∃ u ∈ unitCone, r = (1 - t) • (![1 - eps, 0, 0] : Rate) +
        t • (![0, 1 - eps, -eps] : Rate) + u} := by sorry

end QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Claimed50.P24

end
